=== parameters ===
offline / synthetic only — no broker, no paid API
panel: 50 assets × 600 sessions; weak lagged slow driver; PIT as-of lag=2
shared cost model: 10 bps one-way + IMPACT_K=0.1·σ·√turn (same spirit as P2/P4/P8)
walk-forward: train 240d / test 60d / step 60d; embargo=5; label h=1
look-ahead: signals use shift(1); costs use lagged σ; never join final revision as day-0
cite: Bailey & López de Prado 2014 JPM 40(5) 94–107 — Deflated Sharpe Ratio
cite: AFML (LdP) purged CV / embargo; Perold 1988 FAJ — implementation shortfall
cite: Almgren–Chriss 2000/01 optimal execution intuition; FINRA Notice 26-10 (PDT successor)

=== 1) hypothesis (research brief) ===
  name: slow_momentum_cs_v1
  claim: Cross-sectional ranks of a slow mean-reverting state (lagged 1 day) weakly predict next-day residual returns.
  null: H0: mean daily CS RankIC of lagged slow vs fwd1 = 0 after costs and multiple testing.
  pit_rule: Feature at t uses only information known by close t (slow.shift(1)); as-of alt foil uses lag=2.
  decision_rule: Keep candidate only if sealed OOS mean CS RankIC > 0 AND DSR(N=all_trials) on the SAME net series used for the decision.
  not_advice: Learning exercise on synthetic data — not investment advice.

=== 2) candidate bank (ALL count toward N) ===
explicit N_TRIALS=6 (every scored candidate counts; DSR uses this N on the decision series)

=== 3) walk-forward backtest (shared cost model) ===
folds per candidate ≈ 6; embargo=5

=== 4) sealed OOS evaluation + DSR(N=ALL) on decision series ===
research OOF mean CS IC (honest bank):
  asof_lag2        IC=+0.0467
  slow_lag1        IC=+0.0466
  noise            IC=+0.0120
  mom20            IC=-0.0058
selected=asof_lag2  (LEAK foils excluded from selection but INCLUDED in N=6)
slow_lag1              sealed_IC=+0.0508 net_SR=-0.201 DSR(N=6)=0.000
asof_lag2              sealed_IC=+0.0458 net_SR=-1.484 DSR(N=6)=0.000 <-- SELECTED
rev_final_LEAK         sealed_IC=+0.0519 net_SR=-0.679 DSR(N=6)=0.000
mom20                  sealed_IC=-0.0037 net_SR=-2.796 DSR(N=6)=0.000
noise                  sealed_IC=-0.0172 net_SR=-13.755 DSR(N=6)=0.000
slow_raw_noshift_LEAK  sealed_IC=+0.0528 net_SR=0.586 DSR(N=6)=0.000
teach: DSR on SELECTED series with N=6 → 0.000; same series with dishonest N=1 → 0.156
expected-value context: under H0, max SR across N trials is >0; DSR deflates for that.

=== 5) risk sizing / hard limits ===
vol_target=10% ann; MAX_GROSS=1.5; MAX_NET=0.3; DD_KILL=0.08
sealed sized net_SR=-1.794 maxDD=-0.103 mean_gross=1.500
DD kill would have fired on sealed path? True (engineering switch, not alpha)

=== 6) execution / TCA estimate (Perold IS intuition) ===
notional=$1000000 ADV=$5000000 participation=10%
temp_impact≈37.95 bps  permanent≈18.97 bps  (toy; σ=0.012)
implementation_shortfall≈8.43 bps  +spread 2.0 +fee 1.0 → TCA≈11.43 bps
look-ahead warning: do not size impact with same-bar realized σ; use lagged/ex-ante σ.

